WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:36.780
<b>The Whirl Spider</b>

3
00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.110
I don't have time to fight someone as strong as him!

4
00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.350
I came here to save Ace!

5
00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.000
Gear Second!

6
00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.290
We'll face this guy!

7
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.100
Hawk Eye! Do you remember us?!

8
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.270
We've both challenged you before!

9
00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.250
But now that we're Newkama, we've powered up!

10
00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:32.080
I don't remember the face of every insect I've crushed.

11
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.640
Almost there! Just a little further!

12
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.760
You're still in range.

13
00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.760
T-that hurt...

14
00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.410
He cut me!

15
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.440
Hawk Eye jumped into the air?!

16
00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.690
Damn you!

17
00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.400
Rubber-Rubber...

18
00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:51.650
Jet Bazoo-

19
00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.080
That was too close!

20
00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.250
If I'd stretched my arms, he'd have cut them off!

21
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.760
You aren't as reckless as I expected.

22
00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.850
With just one slash of his sword...

23
00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:39.620
He cut that mountain-sized wall of ice!

24
00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:46.690
S-so this is what the world's mightiest swordsman is capable of.

25
00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:54.100
How freakin' strong is this guy? If he's after Straw Hat, it's all over!

26
00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.940
The ice is falling this way!

27
00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.810
You want me to team up with you?

28
00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:31.590
Stop talking to me as if we were equals.

29
00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.010
You mean you want me to be your underling, right?

30
00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:43.550
Just when I thought Impel Down might have rehabilitated you...

31
00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.180
If it had, I wouldn't have gotten out at all.

32
00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.420
Sandstorm!

33
00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.720
Begone, you damn Flamingo!

34
00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:04.870
And here I thought you'd listen to reason.

35
00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:11.230
As long as I can avoid fighting the marines, this'll all go my way!

36
00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.780
No trouble at all!

37
00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.540
No trouble! No trouble!

38
00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.780
Captain Buggy!

39
00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:28.070
How do you keep getting mixed up in other people's fights like that?!

40
00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.950
Now, what will you do?

41
00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.740
You are being forced further and further away from your brother!

42
00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.390
Damn!

43
00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.960
Is this where it ends?

44
00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:54.210
No trouble!

45
00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.620
It seems that your fighting power has increased considerably,

46
00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.840
but I've already seen through all your tricks.

47
00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.130
From this distance there isn't even a ten thousand to one chance I will miss!

48
00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:07.630
No trouble!

49
00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.630
Rubber-Rubber...

50
00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.800
I'm saved...

51
00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.510
Jet Human Shield!

52
00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:20.320
Hey! What're you doing, Straw Hat?!

53
00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.700
What?! He was the one who cut you!

54
00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:26.320
Besides, didn't you just say you'd come to help me?

55
00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:30.490
You dumbass! You only hear what you want to hear!

56
00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.290
Rubber-Rubber...

57
00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:33.200
Human Shield!

58
00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.200
Cut it out!

59
00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:42.530
Unforgivable! You're Hawk Eye, aren't you?!

60
00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.000
Special Muggy Ball!

61
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.530
Now get blown away!

62
00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.670
Okay, or not.

63
00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:56.410
Do you know why the Muggy Ball is so popular with plumbers?

64
00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:57.800
Why?

65
00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.390
All together now... because it goes...

66
00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.650
Boom!

67
00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:04.810
Wow. Buggyrific!

68
00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.000
Captain Buggy!

69
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.960
Good one!

70
00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.500
Thanks, Buggy!

71
00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.620
I'll never forget you!

72
00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.500
It's not over yet!

73
00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:23.070
Vista! The Old Man ordered us to to keep Ace's brother alive!

74
00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.610
Back him up!

75
00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.800
Understood. I'm on it!

76
00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:39.170
Commander of the Whitebeard Pirates' Fifth Division, Flower Blade Vista.

77
00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:44.530
<b>5th Division Commander of the Whitebeard Pirates
Flower Blade Vista</b>

78
00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:45.120
Nice to meet you, Hawk Eye Mihawk. So you've heard of me?

79
00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.400
It would be strange if I had not.

80
00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:52.700
I'm saved!

81
00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:55.010
Who's that old guy?

82
00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.980
It's not a Devil Fruit, or some cheap trick...

83
00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:00.280
Well, whatever. I'm grateful!

84
00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:10.250
One by one, he turns the people around him into his allies.

85
00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:16.290
Keep going, Straw-Hat-boy!

86
00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.970
Luffy! You must save your brother!

87
00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.690
Move it!

88
00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.740
More than anyone else sailing the seas...

89
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.840
that man possesses the most terrifying power.

90
00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.100
Ace!

91
00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:49.630
As the execution draws ever closer...

92
00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:53.400
a number of shocking truths have been revealed, one after another.

93
00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:05.160
Over two hundred men did the unthinkable and broke out of the impenetrable Impel Down...

94
00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.810
then these infamous, mighty prisoners appeared on the battlefield.

95
00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:18.200
The scene that has unfolded looks like something from a different world.

96
00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:23.390
This truly is an ultimate showdown that will determine the fate of the world!

97
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.500
The people around the world can only hold their breath...

98
00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:32.940
and watch as their futures are decided here.

99
00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:46.110
Fleet Admiral. The preparations are complete.

100
00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.260
The ones for the bay coast as well?

101
00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.820
Yes. They're all ready.

102
00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:55.180
Huh?

103
00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:58.300
They're preparing to execute him...

104
00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.450
They're...

105
00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.110
What are they gonna do to Ace?

106
00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.000
It's not time yet!

107
00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.690
Is the execution gonna start now?

108
00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:15.110
That's impossible! The announced time is still a while off!

109
00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:19.250
Cut the broadcast on all Video Transponder Snails immediately!

110
00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:28.590
For the sake of Absolute Justice, the Navy and the World Government must win this battle at any cost...

111
00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:32.180
regardless of the methods we resort to.

112
00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.650
But this might be too much for the weak-willed commoners to handle.

113
00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:41.990
There's no need to show the world the tragedy about to take place.

114
00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:44.540
Old Man...

115
00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.650
Hurry!

116
00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.880
They really are gonna execute Ace early!

117
00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.790
Ace!

118
00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:01.030
In a few hours we will tell the world...

119
00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:03.500
that we were victorious!

120
00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.030
That's all they need to know.

121
00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:12.940
Our ships were...

122
00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.730
Look at the bay! There's something out there!

123
00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.290
They aren't our allies!

124
00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:38.070
The marines must have circled around behind the frozen waves to come from the coast!

125
00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:42.720
They still have men capable of destroying all those ships?

126
00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:47.640
That's...

127
00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.910
Who are those guys?!

128
00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:58.520
So those are the Government's human weapons that I heard about...

129
00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:08.530
It's those Kuma-looking guys who were at the Sabaody Archipelago...

130
00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.190
There are that many of them?

131
00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:17.870
K-Kuma?

132
00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.940
About an hour and a half after the war began...

133
00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.760
the Navy gambled everything.

134
00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.010
In order to change the flow of the battle...

135
00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:32.070
they plunged into the final phase.

136
00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.120
Now, you guys!

137
00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.260
I was tired of waiting!

138
00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:42.430
It's finally our turn!

139
00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.930
It's the Warlord, Bartholomew Kuma!

140
00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.380
Why are there so many of him?

141
00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.050
What's going on here?!

142
00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:15.860
It's those things that wreaked havoc here on the Sabaody Archipelago a while back!

143
00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:18.930
Multiple Bartholomew Kumas...

144
00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.370
There are even more than there were before!

145
00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.580
Main Office! Main Office!

146
00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.100
Big news!

147
00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.100
Hello? Hello?!

148
00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.990
Is that the real one?

149
00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:52.940
I heard rumors about this.

150
00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:57.170
Doctor Vegapunk has been developing a human weapon.

151
00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:01.060
The prototypes were sent out to deal with various incidents.

152
00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.350
Are these the human weapons?

153
00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.160
Why do they all look like Kuma?

154
00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:11.420
Hey Uncle! This isn't what we planned!

155
00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:18.120
You were supposed to have the pirates surrounded in the bay before we got here,

156
00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.290
but they're scattered all over the place!

157
00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:27.790
I figured out the Navy's plan.

158
00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:33.980
<b>Whitebeard</b>
<b>Allied Ships</b>
<b>Marines</b>

159
00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:36.590
First, they intentionally leaked their plans to execute Ace ahead of schedule, so we'd panic.

160
00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:40.010
After that, the enemy would slowly pull back,

161
00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:43.230
drawing the pirates into the bay after them.

162
00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.840
At that point, the human weapons would block our retreat and we'd be trapped.

163
00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:48.620
<b>Human Weapons</b>

164
00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.350
Checkmate.

165
00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:54.660
So Old Man Whitebeard told us to attack the surrounding ships...

166
00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.130
because he saw this coming.

167
00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:58.960
And because of that, we aren't trapped.

168
00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.010
We may have lost the left and right flanks,

169
00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:08.720
but we can still trap them between us, from the front and back!

170
00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:11.880
Target the supporting pirate crews first, as planned.

171
00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:16.180
Eliminate everyone who slips past our defenses!

172
00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.110
As he says...

173
00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:24.600
Uncle, mind if some of our warships get destroyed, too?

174
00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:27.220
Try to keep it to a minimum.

175
00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:29.410
Roger that.

176
00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:32.220
Let's get going!

177
00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.060
I don't know what's going on...!

178
00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.740
but you won't take us down that easily!

179
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.090
Oh, crap!

180
00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:15.640
Go, Pacifista!

181
00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.460
They got us!

182
00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:02.180
So you don't think twice about sacrificing your own troops.

183
00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.460
Don't falter, men!

184
00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:16.330
Push forward into the plaza!

185
00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.800
All troops, get off the ice!

186
00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:32.020
Do not let the pirates reach the plaza!

187
00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:34.720
Fall back!

188
00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.500
Hurry!

189
00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:53.760
What flower should I make bloom next?

190
00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.270
Drive them in, Pacifista!

191
00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:58.780
As if! Take this!

192
00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:03.720
Serves you right!

193
00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.400
What's with those things?

194
00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.290
It's like they're not even human!

195
00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:22.640
Are they invincible?

196
00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.220
The broadcast...

197
00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:41.760
No matter what you do...

198
00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.080
we still have the upper hand, Whitebeard.

199
00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:51.930
Once all of the broadcasts have been cut, mobilize the enclosure walls!

200
00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:58.500
Then we'll execute Ace and destroy the enemy all at once!

201
00:20:59.100 --> 00:20:59.740
Understood!

202
00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:07.810
Move it!

203
00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:18.420
Ace is in trouble! I gotta hurry!

204
00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.990
Back to where you started from!

205
00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:26.400
Luffy-kun!

206
00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:37.340
Jinbe.

207
00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:44.750
One of the admirals is here...

208
00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:46.970
Dammit!

209
00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.250
He's a formidable foe, but we must hurry!

210
00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:53.060
You always knew that strong enemies would stand in your way,

211
00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:56.820
and you decided to come here anyway, right?!

212
00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:02.930
Die, Dragon's son!

213
00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:13.860
Ace's little brother! Are you already tired?

214
00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:21.260
Oh, it's the Division Commanders!

215
00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:24.190
This makes things easier for us!

216
00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:26.700
You can't let one admiral stop you!

217
00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:27.730
Come with us!

218
00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:30.760
Alright! That bastard!

219
00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:33.350
Now's our chance, while the marines are falling back!

220
00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:35.930
Let's break through their defenses!

221
00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:40.640
Oh, now this looks like a tough bunch!

222
00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:54.180
Commander of the Tenth Division, Curiel!

223
00:22:54.690 --> 00:22:59.160
If you try to attack me, I'll simply crush you!

224
00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:04.060
But just staying in this bay makes your doom inevitable anyway!

225
00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:09.030
Ace will die, and with nowhere to run, you'll all be eliminated!

226
00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:17.140
I don't give a damn who wins, but I'd love to see Whitebeard die!

227
00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:20.930
I won't let the Old Man or Ace die!

228
00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:33.140
Let us put our battle on hold, Vista.

229
00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:37.260
It seems that would benefit us both.

230
00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:47.040
We've been ordered to pull back, Smoker-san.

231
00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:49.140
This area is...

232
00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:52.770
Yeah...

233
00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:54.980
I know.

234
00:23:56.970 --> 00:23:57.950
Straw Hat!

235
00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:08.230
Luffy... hurry to your brother!

236
00:24:14.090 --> 00:24:16.600
Have all the broadcasts been cut?!

237
00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.660
N-No, wait a little longer.

238
00:24:18.660 --> 00:24:20.870
<b>Please stand by.</b>

239
00:24:21.030 --> 00:24:22.170
We're ready over here!

240
00:24:22.280 --> 00:24:23.720
Hey, move over to the side.

241
00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:28.010
I thought one screen was still broadcasting...

242
00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:31.080
Hey! What's going on here?!

243
00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:34.180
Hmm? Who is that over there?

244
00:24:34.970 --> 00:24:38.860
Oh! Is that... Could it be...

245
00:24:38.860 --> 00:24:41.580
A man who hid his identity until now,

246
00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:44.410
but recently revealed himself as part of the legendary crew...

247
00:24:44.410 --> 00:24:47.060
that sailed with the Pirate King Gold Roger!

248
00:24:48.370 --> 00:24:49.100
Who's that?

249
00:24:49.100 --> 00:24:53.090
Is it really that great pirate, Buggy the Clown?!

250
00:24:55.450 --> 00:24:57.860
Yes, it's me alright!

251
00:25:01.840 --> 00:25:05.320
This thing about me being a legendary pirate...

252
00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:07.850
was supposed to be a secret, but...

253
00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:13.010
W-wait, Captain Buggy! You've got a nosebleed!

254
00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:19.450
Cut! Cut!

255
00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:20.530
Wipe your face!

256
00:25:21.400 --> 00:25:23.600
What the hell is this?!

257
00:25:24.160 --> 00:25:28.040
I'm ordering you to cut this ridiculous broadcast!

258
00:25:28.040 --> 00:25:30.920
We can't advance the plan!

259
00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:38.200
W-Well... a Video Transponder Snail was stolen by the Impel Down escapees!

260
00:25:39.220 --> 00:25:41.230
What?!

261
00:25:41.950 --> 00:25:43.350
Makeup!

262
00:25:43.350 --> 00:25:44.990
Okay!

263
00:25:44.990 --> 00:25:46.960
Alright, time for take two!

264
00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:49.710
Three! Two! One!

265
00:25:49.710 --> 00:25:51.080
Go!

266
00:25:51.080 --> 00:25:53.530
Oh! Is that...

267
00:25:54.370 --> 00:25:59.300
the crewmate of the legendary Roger, and blood brother of Red Hair, one of the Four Emperors...

268
00:25:59.980 --> 00:26:03.470
is that the great pirate, Captain Buggy the Clown?

269
00:26:04.130 --> 00:26:05.640
Yes, it's me alright!

270
00:26:06.330 --> 00:26:09.050
Stop them right now!

271
00:26:11.610 --> 00:26:13.180
That was close!

272
00:26:13.180 --> 00:26:15.150
They've found us! Run!

273
00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:21.190
It appeared that you were cut down by Hawk Eye Mihawk,

274
00:26:21.190 --> 00:26:23.160
but you're still standing! Who could you be?

275
00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:25.870
Who, me?

276
00:26:26.850 --> 00:26:28.300
I'm Buggy!

277
00:26:29.600 --> 00:26:31.250
The legend!

278
00:26:31.250 --> 00:26:34.020
Blow them all to pieces!

279
00:26:35.030 --> 00:26:36.710
What's happening on the battlefield?!

280
00:26:36.710 --> 00:26:38.950
Why were the other broadcasts cut?!

281
00:26:38.950 --> 00:26:41.900
Show us Ace. He's about to be executed!

282
00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:44.880
Show us the Bartholomew Kuma army!

283
00:26:49.990 --> 00:26:51.490
Don't give up!

284
00:26:51.490 --> 00:26:55.190
We can't let ourselves be defeated before we've saved Ace!

285
00:26:55.190 --> 00:26:56.820
Let's go!

286
00:26:56.820 --> 00:26:57.930
Yeah!

287
00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:19.020
Old Man...

288
00:27:23.130 --> 00:27:26.150
Squard... You're all right.

289
00:27:26.150 --> 00:27:28.020
Yeah, I survived, somehow.

290
00:27:28.020 --> 00:27:31.720
I see. I tried contacting you earlier...

291
00:27:31.720 --> 00:27:33.930
How are things going in the bay?

292
00:27:33.930 --> 00:27:37.500
Many of our allies are falling.

293
00:27:37.500 --> 00:27:41.700
If the Navy attacks from behind, it'll work to our advantage.

294
00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:46.690
I'm going, too! We've got no choice but to make one last charge!

295
00:27:46.690 --> 00:27:48.210
You're right.

296
00:27:50.540 --> 00:27:52.110
Squard?

297
00:27:52.110 --> 00:27:53.180
What's he doing there?

298
00:27:53.180 --> 00:28:00.860
Forty-three ships are here to back you up. We all owe you a huge debt.

299
00:28:00.860 --> 00:28:04.630
We'd gladly lay down our lives for the Whitebeard Pirates!

